Up-down counter test configuration (updown/)
===========================================

The 'updown' test demonstrates an up-down counter (udcnt_int) instrument that
rises on one event and falls on another.  A single instrument named
'haproxy.sessions.active' tracks how many client sessions are currently open:
it is incremented by one when a client session starts and decremented by one
when that session ends, so its value equals the live session concurrency.

An up-down counter records a signed delta.  The create form of an instrument
supplies one value expression that every 'update' form re-evaluates in the
firing event's context, so the per-event sign is carried through a session
variable: 'set-var' stores +1 in the session_start scope and -1 in the
session_end scope, and the instrument value reads that variable back.  The
filter runs 'set-var' before the instrument within a scope, so the variable
holds the right delta when the measurement is recorded.  A metric value is
always an integer, so the filter coerces the string-typed variable back to
int64 before recording it.


Files
-----

  updown/otel.cfg    OTel filter configuration (instrumentation and two scopes)
  updown/haproxy.cfg HAProxy frontend/backend configuration
  updown/otel.yml    Exporter, reader, processor and provider definitions


Events
------

  on-client-session-start  Stores +1 in the delta variable and adds it to the
                           haproxy.sessions.active counter.
  on-client-session-end    Stores -1 in the delta variable and adds it to the
                           counter.


Instrument
----------

  A create form on session_start registers the instrument; an 'update' form in
  each scope records the signed measurement:

    instrument udcnt_int "haproxy.sessions.active" \
        value var(sess.otel_updown_delta)

  With three concurrent client sessions the counter reads 3, returning to 0
  once they all close.


YAML pipeline
-------------

  Only the metrics signal carries data; traces and logs are wired to /dev/null
  because this test emits neither.

    Signal     Exporter                  Processor / Reader
    --------------------------------------------------------------
    traces     exporter_traces_dev_null  processor_traces_single
    metrics    exporter_metrics_ostream  reader_metrics
    logs       exporter_logs_dev_null    processor_logs_single

  The metrics exporter writes the counter to the __updown_metrics file.  The
  ostream exporter flushes on shutdown, so the recorded value is read there
  after haproxy stops (for example with a 'soft-stop' signal).


Running the test
----------------

The run-updown.sh script (a symlink to run-test-config.sh) runs this
configuration.  It invokes haproxy with -f haproxy-common.cfg -f
updown/haproxy.cfg, the same as the manual command shown below.  From the
test/ directory:

  % ./run-updown.sh

Or run it manually:

  % /path/to/haproxy -f haproxy-common.cfg -f updown/haproxy.cfg
